{
  "_readme": [
    "Text markers looked for in the caption/title/alt text next to a media element.",
    "Matching is case-insensitive with Unicode word boundaries (Cyrillic included);",
    "terms starting with '#' match hashtags.",
    "",
    "Tiers, by what a single hit is worth (see src/core/keywords.ts):",
    "  disclosure - only said when labelling one's own work. 1 hit  -> 'likely' (blocked).",
    "  ambiguous  - reads as a disclosure OR as a topic.     2 hits -> 'likely', 1 -> 'suspected'.",
    "  weak       - suggestive only.                          any   -> 'suspected' (not blocked).",
    "",
    "The split matters: 'AI-generated' belongs in `ambiguous` because a video titled",
    "'AI-generated slop is ruining YouTube' contains exactly the same words as a",
    "disclosure. Putting it in `disclosure` would make that video block itself."
  ],
